{"fail_if": "The 78-80 pre-set, or any plan-derived offered value (including a constant warmup count), survives on any path.", "id": "B3-1", "level": "MUST", "pass_if": "No offered field is ever assigned from the plan or trace; planned sizes use distinct keys (e.g. episode_trace_requests). After prepare_episode returns, every exit from collect() (return or raise) sets offered_requests_from_driver = len(records) of the in-memory episode envelope (prepared.recorder.capture, mutated in place by capture_replay), or 0 if the envelope or records is None. Any warmup offered count likewise comes from the warmup envelope. This is the recorder's offered cohort (one record per accepted offer, each with a fate), not 'sent'. SHOULD: exits before prepare_episode set 0 together with the stage.", "requirement": "Offered accounting from real envelopes (old qualification 78-80)"}
{"fail_if": "An early exit leaves no receipt, a receipt is written after run_episode was entered, or receipt values are derived from the plan.", "id": "B3-2", "level": "MUST", "pass_if": "A try/finally covers from the return of prepare_episode (SHOULD: also prepare raising) to the await of run_episode. An entered flag is set as the last statement before that await, with no intervening await. If not entered, the finally writes an exclusive episode-not-run receipt via services.write (key redaction). It contains: stage; primary exception type and message; prepared.error; envelope status and error; records count 0; the PreparedCapture.started flag if available (client 862; must be False); sent 0. It also persists the prepared capture to a distinct exclusive path, unless adapter prepare-time persistence (U1) is proven by a sealed control. If entered, no NOT_RUN receipt is written (adapter run
{"fail_if": "The write exception surfaces instead of the primary, the primary is missing from the report, or an interrupt is downgraded.", "id": "B3-3", "level": "MUST", "pass_if": "A persist or receipt write failure is recorded (report errors or a write-error file) and never replaces an in-flight primary exception. The primary propagates as the same object, with type and message intact. BaseException (KeyboardInterrupt, SystemExit, CancelledError) is never converted to Exception. With no primary, a persist failure still fails closed (V1). Controls: primary plus write failure; KeyboardInterrupt plus write failure.", "requirement": "Primary exception preserved (L2: warmup finally old 55-64 and the new episode finally)"}
{"fail_if": "Hash and parse use different reads, pins are recorded after traffic, or a mismatch does not refuse. Self-recorded hashes are evidence; the Mayor prereg pin (B1 PRECONDITION) remains the authority.", "id": "B3-4", "level": "MUST", "pass_if": "Before the first capture_replay (the warmup), the caller durably records two things. (a) The sha256 of the protocol bytes it parses (one read; hash and parse the same bytes), compared with the smoke startup pin (old smoke 118-121); a mismatch is refused before any offer. (b) sha256 and resolved path of its own file and of the nominal_episode module actually imported (module object __file__). SHOULD: strict parse (duplicate keys and non-finite constants rejected), and compare the adapter hash with a prereg-supplied expected pin when given.", "requirement": "Pre-traffic pins (B1 residual, L6; old qualification 28, 35)"}
{"fail_if": "A drain is missing, a wait is unbounded, or success is reported with nonzero or unread counters. Only current_in_flight and current_admitted_cost are named in gateway 163-165; the waiting and fallback key names are UNVERIFIED here and must be bound to gateway source at acceptance.", "id": "B3-5", "level": "MUST", "pass_if": "A pre-drain runs after the warmup and before S is chosen; a post-drain runs after run_episode returns or raises. Each is a bounded /metrics read (B3-6) that persists the redacted snapshot and requires: in-flight == 0, waiting == 0 and tokenizer fallback requests == 0 (exact integers), and admitted cost == 0 or a pre-registered |x| <= 1e-9 (I3). A pre-drain failure refuses before S and the permit (NOT_RUN, B3-2). A post-drain failure or skip marks the episode not successful and never replaces a primary exception.", "requirement": "Bounded pre/post drain a
{"fail_if": "A timeout <= 0 is possible, a GET is issued past its bound, or wall-clock time is mixed with the monotonic D/R.", "id": "B3-6", "level": "MUST", "pass_if": "Immediately before each GET, the budget is computed on time.monotonic from the original absolute deadlines: pre-traffic and pre-drain GETs against D - R; the post-drain GET against D - R or, if pre-registered, inside the reserve but never past D. If the budget is <= 0, no GET is issued and a refusal (or NOT_PERFORMED) is recorded; otherwise timeout = min(cap, budget).", "requirement": "Positive, deadline-bounded GET timeouts (L7; old qualification 93)"}
{"fail_if": "S is recomputed or retimed, D or R is replaced, the permit is minted without the coverage check, or a new self-authorization path appears.", "id": "B3-7", "level": "MUST", "pass_if": "Exactly one episode S (monotonic) feeds describe_protocol start_at, the permit (via the protocol sha), NominalRuntime start_at and run_episode offered_start; S is never retimed and there is no second S. The original owner.deadline and owner.reserve go unchanged to the warmup and episode paths. Before minting the permit, the caller checks not_before <= S < expires_at, S + max(episode_s, trace duration_seconds) <= min(D - R, expires_at) and window <= 60 s, and otherwise refuses before traffic. approved=True is set only under --execute, with the external prereg authority reference. Permit limits (window, max_commands, budgets) are not widened unless pre-registered and recorded. SHOULD (L1): record
{"fail_if": "The raw adapter object is stored in report.", "id": "B3-8", "level": "MUST", "pass_if": "The report stores only a strict-JSON copy (json.dumps(sort_keys=True, allow_nan=False) inside a try, then json.loads). On failure it stores a safe summary (error type and message, str keys) and the episode is not successful. Control: a NaN or non-JSON value leaves the terminal report.json writable.", "requirement": "Strict-JSON adapter result (L3; old qualification 128, smoke 327)"}
{"fail_if": "An SDK/gateway label (expected['clock_domain'] or the gateway state label) is passed to capture_replay or compared with a recorder label, or capture['clock_domain'] is rewritten.", "id": "B3-9", "level": "MUST", "pass_if": "Every capture_replay call receives the recorder label (capture['clock_domain'] or nominal_client.clock_domain(); C1-C3). Permit, runtime and gateway checks keep the SDK namespace (prior V5, V6).", "requirement": "Recorder clock label at capture_replay (L5 guard; see l5_erratum)"}
{"fail_if": "Any unlisted change outside these bounds, or a new unredacted write.", "id": "B3-10", "level": "MUST", "pass_if": "The diff touches only the qualification and its test. Sends, schedule, request bodies, fates, the accepted client/metrics/adapter/runtime/permit bytes, and the warmup D/R/persistence (V1, V2) are unchanged. All new writes go through services.write with key redaction (V9).", "requirement": "Role6 scope and invariance"}
{"fail_if": "Not a gate.", "id": "B3-11", "level": "SHOULD", "pass_if": "Optional: also require envelope status 'collected' and records == trace size, and report journal issued_commands. Success is still no claim of cycles or admission effect.", "requirement": "Episode success evidence (prior L8, INFO)"}
DECISION {"PASS_SOURCE": "All MUST rows PASS, critical rows are evidenced (A4) and pins are verified: source acceptance is recommended for the GPU stage. The Mayor decides.", "CONDITIONAL": "All MUST rows PASS by source, but a critical row lacks a control and no witness remains; the gap is listed.", "FAIL": "Any MUST row fails, or there is a scope violation (B2-7, B3-10). Report the smallest exact fix.", "UNVERIFIED": "Never counted as PASS. SHOULD rows never block.", "partial": "A B2-only disposition may be issued while B3 is pending. It never implies caller or native approval."}
